	(text "VERIFICATION STATUS (CLAUDE.md rule 3)\nVERIFIED from Qorvo DW3000 Datasheet v1.1 (local PDF, pdftotext -raw for\nTable 2): pin functions, SPI-mode straps (Table 20), WAKEUP/RSTn/IRQ/SYNC\nhandling, RF1/RF2 requirements, Fig 32 passive values (rendered image).\nNOT re-verified this pass: v1.3 of the datasheet (Qorvo download rate-\nlimited). The XTO 1pF requirement is quoted from v1.3 in positioning.md;\nv1.1 does not state it.\nNOT OBTAINED: DW3000 User Manual (SYNC/OSTR). Hence SYNC is DNP.\nOPEN: DW3210 exposed pad net; whether four RSTn pins tied together can\ncontend while one chip is still in POR (each pin is an O-H output); BLM03\ncase size (Murata BLM03 = 0201 by Murata naming, components.csv says\n0402) -- FB1-FB4 footprint left blank until checked."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.74 325.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0d34268f-0100-466e-a1b4-2a3bc8fd8865")
	)
	(text "U7 = A3  OUTER anchor\nTDoA vs A0 -> DIRECTION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 472.44 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1984a20a-72b9-46fa-86f0-7bb38e09eab3")
	)
	(text "U6 = A2  OUTER anchor\nTDoA vs A0 -> DIRECTION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 332.74 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "38ba4a05-eb1e-4791-aeb4-666026d1c316")
	)
	(text "BRING-UP TESTS FOR THIS SHEET (details in uwb_array_notes.md)\n 1. Rails: +3V3_A0..A3 at TP500/407/414/421; current per anchor via R200-R203.\n 2. Clock at every XTI (TP6-TP9 on testpoints) BEFORE expecting SPI: the\n    core is held in reset until the oscillator is stable (DS v1.1 s6).\n 3. SPI DEV_ID read on each CS in turn, mode 0, start at 2MHz then raise.\n    A wrong-mode read returns shifted garbage on all four the same way.\n 4. Release UWB_RST_N; confirm every IRQ idles low (R25-R28).\n 5. CW / continuous-frame TX per anchor into a spectrum analyser at the SMA\n    (conducted). Compare the four: same power within ~1dB or a path is off.\n 6. Loopback: A0 TX -> attenuator -> A1 RX by cable; repeat each pair.\n 7. Skew: one tag at a fixed, surveyed position; log RX timestamps on all\n    four for N frames; per-anchor offsets must be stable to <~30ps over\n    temperature/time -- the absolute value calibrates out, drift does not."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 391.16 325.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "60372215-e30b-4a43-b766-6738ea2def37")
	)
	(text "UWB Array -- 4x DW3210: A0 = CENTER (TWR, range), A1-A3 = OUTER (TDoA vs A0, direction)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66666666-0000-4000-8000-000000000001")
	)
	(text "THE FOUR ANCHORS ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE PEERS.\n  U4 = A0, the CENTER anchor: two-way ranging with the wristband -> RANGE.\n  U5-U7 = A1-A3, the OUTER anchors: timestamp the SAME tag frame, TDoA vs A0\n          -> DIRECTION. One tag transmission, four measurements.\n  CS0/IRQ0/UWB_CLK0/J20 are A0. Index n = anchor An everywhere on this sheet.\nWhy discrete DW3210 (QFN40, non-PDoA) and not DWM3000 modules: TDoA needs one\ntime base and the module has no clock pin. XTI (pin 21) is an \"external\nreference overdrive pin\" (DS Table 2); all four are driven from clock_dist.\n\nWIRED 2026-11-17 against docs/net-contract.md. Per anchor:\n  SPICLK/MOSI/MISO 34/35/36 -> shared UWB_SCK/MOSI/MISO.\n  SPICSn 37 -> 0R (R204-R207) -> UWB_CSn_N.   (internal pull-up, DS s4.9.5)\n  IRQ 1 -> 100k pull-down R25-R28 (DS Table 2: floats in SLEEP) and\n          0R R208-R211 -> UWB_IRQn.\n  RSTn 33 -> 0R R212-R215 -> shared UWB_RST_N. Open-drain from the host only:\n          \"Must not be pulled high by external source\" (DS Table 2). No pull-up.\n  WAKEUP 32 -> shared UWB_WAKEUP, 100k pull-down R224 (DS: ground if unused).\n  GPIO7/SYNC 9 -> DNP 0R R216-R219 -> UWB_SYNC. Internally pulled down.\n  EXTON 31, GPIO0-4 (3,4,6,7,8) -> test pads TP500-TP527 only.\n  RF2 13 -> 49R9 R33-R36 to GND on a 50 ohm trace (non-PDoA, DS Table 2)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66666666-0000-4000-8000-000000000002")
	)
	(text "SPI MODE: R10-R17 are 10k PULL-DOWNS on GPIO5/SPIPOL (pin 5) and\nGPIO6/SPIPHA (pin 2), sampled at power-up (DS v1.1 Fig 21). 0/0 = SPI MODE 0\n(DS v1.1 Table 20). Mode 0 is also the internal-pull default (\"internally\npulled low to configure a default SPI mode 0\"), so the externals only make\nit deterministic. FIRMWARE MUST USE MODE 0 (CPOL=0, CPHA=0). 36MHz max in\nmode 0, 20MHz in CRC mode (Table 19).\n  R10/R11 = A0 GPIO5/6, R12/R13 = A1, R14/R15 = A2, R16/R17 = A3.\n\nSUPPLIES (\"lowest BOM\" scheme, DS v1.1 Fig 32, all rails 3.3V):\n  +3V3 -> 0R R200-R203 (per-anchor current break, TP on +3V3_An) -> VDD1 29,\n  VDD2b 23, VDD3 26.  VDD2a 28 via its own BLM03PG330SN1D bead FB1-FB4\n  (\"F-15 requires isolation with a ferrite from B-15\", Table 2).\n  VTX_D 27 and VIO_D 38 are decoupling-only pins: cap to GND, never a rail.\n  Every decoupling cap carries a 'Placement' field naming the pin it serves,\n  because VDD1/VDD2b/VDD3 share one net here. Smaller cap nearest the pad.\n  Shared bank C72-C74 at the array entry = Fig 32 C6/C7/C8.\n\nCLOCK: XTI 21 <- UWB_CLKn (2200pF AC cap lives on clock_dist). XTO 22 ->\n1pF C28-C31 to GND (moved here from clock_dist to sit at the pin).\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.74 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66666666-0000-4000-8000-000000000003")
	)
	(text "RF PATH, drawn IDENTICALLY for all four anchors (layout must match):\n  RF1 18 -> 2.0pF C47/C55/C63/C71 (part of the simulated line, do not swap)\n  -> DNP shunt -> 0R series -> DNP shunt  (pi-match, 0402 in-track)\n  -> J20-J23 SMA edge (Linx/TE CONSMA020.042-G, 0-18GHz, for 0.042in PCB;\n     this board is 1.048mm. 5-7.125GHz: IL 0.23dB, VSWR 1.1 max).\n  RF1 is 50 ohm single-ended (DS Table 2) -- NO balun. No filter: DS Fig 32\n  note says a BPF \"may be required for certification in some regions\";\n  the pi-match pads can take one. Qorvo shows no ESD part; the\n  connector-side shunt pad accepts an 0402 RF ESD diode if needed.\n  CONDUCTED TEST: the SMA IS the conducted port. No u.FL/MMCX on this path\n  (CH5 6489.6MHz is above their 6GHz rating).\n\nLENGTH MATCHING (precision-critical, docs/positioning.md):\n  1cm of differential path = ~10cm of position error at 10m.\n  - RF1 -> SMA: same geometry, same length, same via count on all four.\n    Mismatch calibrates out but only if it is stable; keep it small anyway.\n  - UWB_CLK0..3 buffer -> XTI: equal length (clock_dist).\n  - Coax + antenna: matched set, captive if possible.\nLAYOUT (DS s7.3): 50 ohm RF lines; 2pF pads at track width; ground removed\nunder the chip on F.Cu + In1.Cu; first solid ground on In2.Cu.\nEXPOSED PAD: the QFN footprint has an EP but the DW3210 symbol has 40 pins\nand DS v1.1 Table 2 does not name the EP. Resolve (Fig 38 / Qorvo) before\nlayout -- it is almost certainly GND but that is NOT verified."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 391.16 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "90a8c0c6-28f5-4b3a-ac27-fe901b5aa2b0")
	)
	(text "U5 = A1  OUTER anchor\nTDoA vs A0 -> DIRECTION"
